Symbolic links named like C headers below testdata, one to a named pipe the test
makes and one to a device, beside a header that names a function. Reading either
link would block or never end, and neither is a file a compiler reads, so the run
reads neither and retains only what the header names.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/pipe

go 1.27.0
-- docs/names.h --
void named(void);
-- testdata/p.h.symlink --
pipe
-- testdata/z.h.symlink --
/dev/zero
-- main.go --
package main

var named, spare int

func main() {}
